WEBVTT

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:30.688
I found out that my dad,
who I was very, very close to, was gay.

00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:32.990
I was taken completely by surprise.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.498
We were a very tight-knit family,

00:00:35.498 --> 00:00:37.889
and I was crushed.

00:00:37.889 --> 00:00:40.234
At some point, in one
of our strained conversations,

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.904
my dad mentioned the Stonewall riots.

00:00:42.904 --> 00:00:46.178
He told me that one night in 1969,

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.883
a group of young black
and Latino drag queens

00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:52.529
fought back against the police
at a gay bar in Manhattan

00:00:52.529 --> 00:00:54.549
called the Stonewall Inn,

00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:58.078
and how this sparked
the modern gay rights movement.

00:00:58.078 --> 00:01:01.417
It was an amazing story,
and it piqued my interest.